.TH VIGIL-ASK 1 2026-10-31 "VIGIL OS" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vigil-ask \- ask a quick question from the desktop
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vigil-ask
.RB [ window ]
.RB [ \-\-selection ]
.RB [ \-\-file
.IR FILE ]...
.RB [ \-\-history
.IR ID " | " \-\-last ]
.br
.B vigil-ask prompt
.br
.B vigil-ask history
.br
.B vigil-ask ask
.RB [ \-\-selection ]
.RB [ \-\-file
.IR FILE ]...
.RB [ \-\-resume
.IR SESSION ]
.RI [ QUESTION ...| \- ]
.br
.B vigil-ask status
.RB [ \-\-follow ]
.RB [ \-\-polybar ]
.br
.B vigil-ask cancel
.SH DESCRIPTION
VIGIL Ask answers quick questions in a small window shared by the Plasma and i3 editions.
It uses Claude Code by Anthropic, so questions and anything attached to them are processed in the cloud under your Claude account.
Claude Code needs a paid Claude plan or a Claude Console account.
.PP
In VIGIL Ask, Claude Code runs with no tools, no MCP servers and none of your Claude Code settings, from an empty folder of its own.
It can answer, but it cannot run commands, read or change files, or browse.
For hands-on work, \fBOpen in Claude Code\fR starts an interactive session in a folder you choose, with the question typed in but not sent.
.PP
Nothing is collected in the background.
The selection and files are attached only when you ask for them, and you see each attachment before anything is sent.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B window
Open the window, or bring the open one forward.
\fB\-\-selection\fR attaches the primary selection, \fB\-\-file\fR attaches a UTF-8 text file of up to 512 KiB,
\fB\-\-history\fR reopens a conversation from history and \fB\-\-last\fR the most recent one.
.TP
.B prompt
Ask through a Rofi prompt and show the answer in the window.
.TP
.B history
Pick a recent conversation in Rofi.
.TP
.B ask
Ask in the terminal and print the answer as it arrives. The session ID is printed last, for \fB\-\-resume\fR.
.TP
.B status
Print idle, working, done, stopped, failed, signin, missing or off. It never includes question text.
.TP
.B cancel
Stop the question being answered, in the window or in a terminal. The i3 edition runs this before locking and when you log out.
.SH DESKTOP
On i3, Super+Shift+A asks through Rofi and Super+Ctrl+A opens the window with the selection attached.
The Polybar module shows the status; click it to ask, middle-click for history and right-click to reopen the last conversation.
In Thunar, \fBSend To\fR > \fBVIGIL Ask\fR attaches the selected text files.
.SH FIRST USE
If Claude Code is missing, the window offers to install it from Anthropic's signed repository,
\fI/etc/yum.repos.d/claude-code.repo\fR, which ships turned off.
Installing asks for an administrator password, then turns the repository on so Claude Code updates with the rest of the system.
Before the first question the window explains where questions go, and it opens a terminal for \fBclaude auth login\fR when you need to sign in.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/vigil-ask/config.json
\fBenabled\fR (true), \fBhistory_days\fR (30; 0 keeps no history), \fBmodel\fR (Claude Code's default when null) and \fBnotice_accepted\fR.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/vigil-ask/history.json
Recent questions and answers, readable only by you.
.TP
.I ~/.claude
Claude Code's own transcripts, kept by Claude Code.
.TP
.I /etc/vigil-ask/disabled
When this file exists, VIGIL Ask is off for every user.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR claude (1)
